{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8afa843992ea5b40cbddbef4dd2871f7259bd2ceb30ca3723cc632ab79da1e7e","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate / project portability criterion","key_entities":[".rebar/prompts/plan-review-project-portability.md",".rebar/criteria_routing.json","project.portability","tests/unit/test_project_portability_criterion.py","tests/unit/test_project_portability_docs.py","docs/plan-review-gate.md","AGENTS.md","Platform and venue matrix cell","rebar explain","rebar review-plan"],"problem_keywords":["portability","CI provider independence","plan-review criterion","no CI provider fallback","GitHub Actions dependency"],"propositions":["The portability criterion's Platform and venue matrix cell conflates CI under any provider with no CI provider, leaving the no-CI-provider shape unnameable and undetectable by the reviewer.","A capability whose only trigger is a specific CI system (e.g. GitHub Actions schedule) is not portable; such a plan needs an operation-linked or in-process fallback or it fails when no CI provider is present.","The authoritative portability rule must be stated once in .rebar/prompts/plan-review-project-portability.md and mirrored in docs/plan-review-gate.md with tests pinning both.","Live A/B testing confirms that under the updated rubric, a GitHub-Actions-only compaction trigger with no fallback now emits a project.portability finding naming the no-CI-provider alternate shape, whereas the pre-change rubric emitted none."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787807207643668001,"uuid":"70ea6c08-bb8d-4033-ac19-6a7e2ddd